{
  "abstract": "The auxiliary results of Plantholt and Shan's proof of the asymptotic overfull conjecture (arXiv:2105.05286, Section 2), in Lean 4 / Mathlib, as a first version of a package that will add their Theorems 1.2 and 1.3. hakimi (Theorem 2.5, Hakimi 1962): d : V → ℕ is the degree function of a loopless multigraph (symmetric multiplicities with zero diagonal) iff ∑ d is even and 2 d v ≤ ∑ d for every v. hamiltonConnected_of_minDegree (Theorem 2.6, Hamilton-connected part, in the form δ ≥ n/2 + 1): a graph on n ≥ 5 vertices with n + 2 ≤ 2δ has a Hamiltonian path between any two distinct vertices (Dirac's theorem on G − u − v, from the registered menger-hamiltonian entry, and a pigeonhole choice of consecutive cycle neighbours). exists_spanning_paths (Lemma 2.12): for t + 1 pairs (aᵢ, bᵢ) of vertices, all distinct, in a graph with n + 6(t + 1) + 2 ≤ 2δ and 3(t + 1) + 5 ≤ n, there are pairwise vertex-disjoint paths from aᵢ to bᵢ covering all vertices (join a₀, b₀ through a common neighbour, delete the three vertices, recurse; the last pair is joined by a Hamiltonian path). One definition (IsMultigraph). Three statements.",
